    "title": "Plan import --update replaces all ACs instead of merging. When extending an existing spec with a new",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "Plan import --update replaces all ACs instead of merging. When extending an existing spec with a new AC via plan import, --update overwrites acceptance_criteria entirely. Need AC-merge strategy: append new AC IDs, preserve existing ones. Encountered during spec-plan for session-log-show ac-10.",
    "spec_ref": "@plan-import",
    "status": "pending",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-26T19:32:59.586Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJDQ8ZD10EG4Z7MHEAHWBMAT",
        "created_at": "2026-02-26T19:37:08.769Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\n\n**What**: When `kspec plan import --update` encounters an existing spec, it replaces the entire `acceptance_criteria` array instead of merging. If a spec already has ac-1 through ac-9 and a plan adds ac-10, --update overwrites all ACs with only what the plan document contains, losing ac-1 through ac-9.\n\n**Where**: `src/cli/commands/plan-import.ts` lines 271-303 (the --update branch). The update logic builds a `Partial<SpecItemInput>` and sets `updates.acceptance_criteria = spec.acceptance_criteria` (line 296), passed to `updateSpecItem()` in `src/parser/yaml.ts` line 1522. `updateSpecItem` does direct property assignment (`targetObj[key] = value` at line 1560) with no merge logic.\n\n**How**: Implement an AC merge strategy in the update path. When `updates.acceptance_criteria` is set and the existing item already has ACs:\n1. Index existing ACs by their `id` field (e.g., \"ac-1\", \"ac-2\")\n2. For each AC in the plan update: if an AC with the same `id` exists, replace it; otherwise append it\n3. Preserve existing ACs whose IDs are not in the update set\nBest done in `plan-import.ts` before calling `updateSpecItem`, since general updateSpecItem callers may want full replacement semantics.\n\n**Done when**:\n- `kspec plan import --update` with a plan that adds one new AC to an existing spec preserves all pre-existing ACs and appends the new one\n- A plan that modifies an existing AC (same id) updates that AC in place while preserving others\n- Tests cover: append-only new AC, update existing AC by id, mixed append+update, no ACs in plan (preserves existing), empty existing ACs (creates all from plan)",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "automation": "eligible",
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
